[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Network Interception and Request/Response Mocking in Playwright"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Playwright provides powerful capabilities to intercept, modify, and mock network traffic. This allows developers to test their applications against various API scenarios, simulate error states, and speed up tests by avoiding reliance on real backend services."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding page.route()"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"The core of network interception in Playwright is the page.route() method. It allows you to match specific URL patterns and intercept requests before they reach the server."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"await page.route('**/api/v1/users', async route => {
  // Handle the intercepted route
});"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"Mocking API Responses"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can fulfill an intercepted request with custom data using the route.fulfill() method. This is useful for returning predefined JSON payloads without hitting the actual database."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"await page.route('**/api/v1/user-profile', async route => {
  await route.fulfill({
    status: 200,
    contentType: 'application/json',
    body: JSON.stringify({ id: 1, name: 'Jane Doe', role: 'admin' })
  });
});"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"Modifying Requests Before Forwarding"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Sometimes you want to let the request go through to the server, but you need to alter headers, post data, or query parameters. You can achieve this using route.continue()."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"await page.route('**/api/data', async route => {
  const headers = {
    ...route.request().headers(),
    'x-test-header': 'playwright-automation'
  };
  await route.continue({ headers });
});"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Simulating Network Failures and Error Codes"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Robust frontend applications must handle server errors gracefully. Playwright makes it easy to simulate 500 Internal Server Errors, 404 Not Found, or complete network failures."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"await page.route('**/api/v1/settings', async route => {
  await route.fulfill({
    status: 500,
    body: 'Internal Server Error'
  });
});"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use wildcards or regular expressions in route patterns to target multiple endpoints."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always call either route.fulfill(), route.continue(), or route.abort() to prevent hanging network requests."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Combine network mocking with UI assertions to verify that loading spinners, error banners, and fallback data render correctly."}]
